WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.380
Does "The Way of Water" circle&nbsp;
down a plothole-sized drain in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.740
its final act? Or are some fans&nbsp;
missing the ocean for the waves?

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.960
After keeping fans waiting for 13 years, James&nbsp;
Cameron's "Avatar: The Way of Water" has arrived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.580
in theaters. The film sees Jake Sully and his&nbsp;
family leaving the sanctity of their forest home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.860
to live with an ocean tribe of Na'vi people in&nbsp;
order to escape a vengeful Colonel Miles Quaritch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:28.020
The sequel began development shortly after the&nbsp;
monumental 2009 release of the first "Avatar."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:33.555
Following a series of delays, the film is finally&nbsp;
out for the world to see in all its 3D glory.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.080
"Let's get it done."

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.560
While the first "Avatar" has never been seen as a&nbsp;
groundbreaking feat of storytelling, the visuals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.660
and worldbuilding introduced in it have been more&nbsp;
than enough to satisfy moviegoers. This appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.520
to be the case for its sequel as well, with its&nbsp;
Rotten Tomatoes consensus calling it "a stunningly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.140
immersive experience." But it seems that even&nbsp;
the most jaw-dropping visuals on earth can do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:00.300
little to hide a notable plot hole regarding the&nbsp;
film's final act that fans simply cannot ignore.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.400
The third act of "The Way of Water" centers on&nbsp;
a grand battle between the Na'vi and Colonel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.740
Quaritch's gang. But for those who think that the&nbsp;
newly-introduced Metkayina Na'vi ocean tribe would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.960
be by Jake Sully's side, think again. On a Reddit&nbsp;
thread discussing the film, one user points out,

00:01:20.787 --> 00:01:24.960
They go on to describe how the Metkayina&nbsp;
disappear following their fight to protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.807
the whale-like Tulkuns, leaving Sully and his&nbsp;
family to go against Quaritch's gang alone.

00:01:29.807 --> 00:01:33.552
"I need you with me."

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:36.600
Other fans chimed in, coming up&nbsp;
with their own justifications for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.540
the absence of the Metkayina&nbsp;
during the fight. Many saw it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.080
as the Metkayina people looking out for&nbsp;
themselves, like this user, who posted,

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.664
Another Redditor agreed, writing,

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:57.120
However, another user offered a solid rebuttal,&nbsp;
seeing the storytelling purpose for this, posting,

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.960
"Honestly, I think it was an intended plot&nbsp;
hole because Cameron wanted to focus on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.560
family unit ... All of that would have&nbsp;
been [moot] had the sea tribe stayed."

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.420
While the Metkayina could have had a more active&nbsp;
hand in the final act of "Avatar: The Way of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.440
Water," this is far from a reflection of their&nbsp;
involvement throughout the rest of the franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.880
With the end of "Way of Water" confirming that&nbsp;
the Metkayina will be helping Jake Sully in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.560
ongoing battle against humanity and director James&nbsp;
Cameron confirming that "Avatar 3" will be coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.240
out, it seems that we've only touched the surface&nbsp;
of what the water-bound tribe has to offer.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.320
Kate Winslet, who portrays the Metkayina&nbsp;
chief's wife Ronal in "Way of Water,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.460
says that her character, in particular, is a&nbsp;
crucial piece of the puzzle in the future of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.000
the "Avatar" universe. In an interview&nbsp;
with Variety, the "Titanic" star said,

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:50.460
James Cameron and pulse-pounding finales are a&nbsp;
match made in heaven, so hopefully, whatever the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.780
Metkayina tribe have up their slippery sleeves&nbsp;
will make up for any plot hole complaints.

